{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 26, :comments ["<b>And these are the sons of Dishan: Hemdan and Eshban</b> — This is Dishon, the fifth son of Seir, for there is no concern that he be called Dishan or Dishon except when they are in a single verse, to distinguish between the two. Similarly, <b>\"And Hiram made the basins, and Hiram finished</b>\" (I Kings 7:40) [where the name appears in two forms]. And Scripture found it necessary here to call him Dishan, so that it not be assumed that he is Dishon the son of Anah mentioned just above, when genealogizing his descendants, for so it would be understood."], :book :genesis, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 36, :notes {0 "The cited verse reference I Kings 7:40 is inferred from the quoted phrase; the Hebrew text gives only the abbreviation מלכים א ז מ."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:40:35.885564898Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}